## The Danger of Blind Unwrap

```xiom
fn get_name(user_id: Int) -> Str {
  let user = find_user(user_id);  // Returns Option[User]
  return user.unwrap().name;      // CRASH if user is None!
}
```

### Contract-Guarded Unwrap
```xiom
fn safe_unwrap[T](opt: Option[T]) -> T
  requires: opt.is_some();
  ensures: result == opt.unwrap();
{ return opt.unwrap(); }
```

### Better: Match Instead of Unwrap
```xiom
fn get_name(user_id: Int) -> Str {
  let user = find_user(user_id);
  return match user {
    Some(u) => u.name,
    None => "Unknown User",
  };
}
```

### When Unwrap IS Safe
```xiom
fn process(items: &Vec[Int]) -> Int
  requires: items.len() > 0;
{
  let first = items.first();  // Returns Option[Int]
  return first.unwrap();       // Safe: we know items is non-empty
}
```

### Contract Chaining
```xiom
fn lookup_then_unwrap[K: Eq, V](map: &Map[K, V], key: K) -> V
  requires: map.contains(key);
  ensures: result == map.get(key).unwrap();
{ return map.get(key).unwrap(); }
```

### The Pattern
Don't unwrap unless you can PROVE the value exists — either through a contract or a preceding check.

